实体与目标实体不同\"}, {\"retryable\": true, \"source_skill\": \"coverage_attribution_audit\", \"code\": \"REQUIRED_ITEM_MISSING\", \"provenance\": \"environment/files/Birchwood/PackageA/06_Submittals_RFI/RFI_Log_PackageA.xlsx:L39\", \"blocking\": true, \"claim_id\": \"FILL_RFI_079\", \"message\": \"Check stockpile approval scope and gradation retest\", \"requirement_id\": \"RFI_079\"}, {\"retryable\": false, \"source_skill\": \"engineering_solver\", \"code\": \"SOLVER_EVIDENCE_MISSING\", \"blocking\": true, \"message\": \"A stockpile-specific laboratory determination remains unverified.\"}, {\"retryable\": true, \"source_skill\": \"entity_provenance_audit\", \"code\": \"AUTHORITY_REFERENCE_UNVERIFIED\", \"blocking\": true, \"claim_id\": \"FILL_RFI_079\", \"message\": \"FILL_RFI_079 的出处在本轮权威证据中无法核验\"}], \"repair_claim_ids\": [\"FILL_RFI_079\", \"FILL_TEST_BASIS\"], \"reason\": \"FILL_ACTIONABLE_EVIDENCE\"}","draft_output":"1. PURPOSE\nReview the Block A slab-on-grade compaction record for Item 054.\n2. DOCUMENTS REVIEWED\nBlock A Placement Records, VMT-25-0918-P04, RFI Log and Earth Moving Rev 3.\n3. BASIS OF REVIEW\nSection 31 20 00 requires ASTM D1557 Method C on material actually placed. [environment/files/Birchwood/PackageA/03_Specifications/Spec_312000_Earth_Moving_Rev3.pdf:L68]\n4. FINDINGS\nThe placement log identifies the Stockpile north of Block C [environment/tools/files/ce01-slab-on-grade-fill-compaction-acceptance-3d2c133e/Fill_Placement_Records_BlockA_SlabOnGrade.xlsx:L23]. VMT-25-0918-P04 tested Larchwood Pit [environment/files/Birchwood/PackageA/04_Materials/Proctor_D1557_PackageA_Structural_Fill.pdf:L24]. A matching D1557 Method C determination has not been established in the reviewed files. Density and moisture acceptance limits remain undetermined for the material placed.\nRFI 079 approved reuse of the Stockpile north of Block C subject to a gradation retest, referencing TPM-25-079 [environment/files/Birchwood/PackageA/06_Submittals_RFI/RFI_Log_PackageA.xlsx:L39]. The closed entry establishes the RFI disposition. It does not document completion of the gradation retest. Obtain and verify that retest before acceptance.\n5. CONCLUSION AND RECOMMENDATION\nItem 054 remains open.","route_status":"RETRY_CONFLICT","targeted_evidence":{"FILL_RFI_079":[{"score":22,"path":"environment/files/Birchwood/PackageA/06_Submittals_RFI/RFI_Log_PackageA.xlsx","start_line":37,"excerpt":"L37: RFI 052 | 08/22/2025 | Geotechnical | Rowan Bay Constructors | Lift thickness for engineered fill over Block B clay | 12 in loose lift maximum; 14 lifts to reach El. 750.0 | Thelbridge (R. Nimkar) | 08/28/2025 | Closed\nL38: RFI 065 | 09/16/2025 | Geotechnical | Rowan Bay Constructors | Field density test frequency requirements | One test per 500 sf per lift, plus one at each transition — per Spec 31 20 00 | Thelbridge (K. Tarbray) | 09/22/2025 | Closed\nL39: RFI 079 | 10/06/2025 | Geotechnical | Rowan Bay Constructors | Approval of borrow stockpile north of Block C for reuse | Approved subject to gradation retest; see letter TPM-25-079 | Thelbridge (R. Nimkar) | 10/10/2025 | Closed\nL40: RFI 093 | 10/23/2025 | Geotechnical | Rowan Bay Constructors | Piezometer PZ-3 reading discrepancy 10/17 vs. 10/20 | Reading within instrument tolerance; no action | Kelbrook Geotechnical | 10/28/2025 | Closed","end_line":40},{"score":13,"path":"environment/tools/files/ce01-slab-on-grade-fill-compaction-acceptance-3d2c133e/Fill_Placement_Records_BlockA_SlabOnGrade.xlsx","start_line":69,"excerpt":"L69: 4 | Structural fill for this pad was drawn from the stockpile north of Block C, approved for reuse under RFI 079 (closed 10/10/2025). Haul was by on-site scraper and articulated truck from the stockpile face; no off-site delivery tickets apply to this work.\nL70: 5 | Governing laboratory Proctor carried on this record is Vantree Materials Testing Report VMT-25-0918-P04 dated 09/18/2025, ASTM D1557 Method C, γd,max = 128.4 pcf, wopt = 9.2%, as used on the Block B mass fill record RB-FPR-BB-2025.\nL71: 6 | Lift acceptance: each lift was tested by Vantree Materials Testing before the succeeding lift was placed, in accordance with Specification Section 31 20 00 Article 1.6.B. Field density reports were issued lift-by-lift as FDR-BA-01 through FDR-BA-05, three tests per lift; Lift 6 results are reported in Field Density Report SF-26-0708.\nL72: 7 | Weather: no full shifts lost. Ambient temperatures ran high through the placement period and surface moisture loss between spreading and rolling was noted by the field engineer on 06/26 and 06/30.","end_line":72},{"score":12,"path":"environment/tools/files/ce01-slab-on-grade-fill-compaction-acceptance-3d2c133e/Fill_Placement_Records_BlockA_SlabOnGrade.xlsx","start_line":21,"excerpt":"L21: Nominal lift thickness | 8 in loose; ~7.2 in compacted\nL22: Plan area of pad | 11,400 sf (Block A slab-on-grade footprint, grids B-G / 1-5)\nL23: Borrow source | Stockpile north of Block C - approved for reuse per RFI 079\nL24: Governing Proctor reference | Vantree Materials Testing Report VMT-25-0918-P04, ASTM D1557 Method C, γd,max = 128.4 pcf, wopt = 9.2%","end_line":24}],"FILL_TEST_BASIS":[{"score":21,"path":"environment/files/Birchwood/PackageA/00_Program/Thelbridge_Verification_Register_PkgA.xlsx","start_line":81,"excerpt":"L81: 051 | Geotechnical | Design | Item 051 | KGI-2024-0417 Rev.2, VMT-2025-0109-CON, Calculation CB-GEO-007, Verification Register — Package A, Specification Section 31 20 00, Settlement Monitoring Records — Block C, Geotechnical Index Test Data | Verify Block C spread-footing foundations for long-term settlement over the compressible CL clay (Cc 0.28, e0 0.92, σ'p 1,900 psf; 18 ft layer) with stress increase Δσ 900 psf at mid-layer against settlement tolerance 1 in total / 0.5 in differential. Verify that the settlement analysis is complete and reconciled against the project tolerances; correlate with monitoring reading of 0.61 in cumulative on 06/26/2026. | R. Nimkar (Thelbridge