2026 recommends rejection of Set 3 on the basis of the reported 4,620 psi test average. | K. Tarbray (Thelbridge) | 07/07/2026 | Assigned to Karen Tarbray — Materials / QA Reviewer. Hold-point critical. Materials acceptance record pending. Required by 07/20/2026. | K. Tarbray (Thelbridge) | — | Open | —\nL84: 054 | Materials | Materials | Item 054 | Proctor D1557 — Package A Structural Fill, Field Density Report SF-26-0708, Verification Register — Package A, Pour-Readiness Notification 07/14/2026, Specification Section 31 20 00, Proctor D698 — Phase 1 Borrow | Accept or reject slab-on-grade fill compaction Tests FD-14 through FD-17 (Field Density Report SF-26-0708, ASTM D6938 nuclear gauge, tests 07/08/2026, report 07/09/2026). Compaction requirement per Spec 31 20 00 Article 3.4.B. Verify that the field density results are evaluated against the appropriate laboratory reference compaction standard for this fill. | K. Tarbray (Thelbridge) | 07/09/2026 | Assigned to Karen Tarbray — Materials / QA Reviewer. Materials acceptance record pending. Required by 07/20/2026. | K. Tarbray (Thelbridge) | — | Open | —","end_line":84},{"score":20,"path":"environment/tools/files/ce01-slab-on-grade-fill-compaction-acceptance-3d2c133e/Fill_Placement_Records_BlockA_SlabOnGrade.xlsx","start_line":25,"excerpt":"L25: Compaction acceptance basis | Specification Section 31 20 00, Article 3.4.B\nL26: Subgrade preparation | Topsoil and existing uncontrolled fill stripped to El. 745.0; subgrade proof-rolled 06/18/2026 with loaded tandem-axle dump truck in the presence of Vantree Materials Testing; written acceptance issued by Thelbridge Project Management Services, memo TPM-26-063 dated 06/18/2026\nL27: Production test strip | Executed 06/19/2026 at the north end of the pad, witnessed by Vantree Materials Testing and Thelbridge Project Management Services; established 6 coverage passes of the CS56B smooth-drum with pneumatic follow-pass at 8 in loose lift thickness for production placement\nL